*.wyn.c
*.wyn.out
*.out
# ...but wynjs's expected-output FIXTURES are source, not build output. They
# happen to end in .out and the blanket rule above was swallowing all 20 of them,
# so the repo shipped every .js case with no way to know what it should print:
# a fresh clone could not run wynjs's suite at all. The runner reads these files
# (tests/test_main.wyn: `want = File.read(want_path)`), and each one is generated
# from REAL node output, which is the only reason the suite can detect a wrong
# EXPECTATION rather than just a wrong result.
!wynjs/tests/cases/*.out
*.dSYM/
.DS_Store
# compiled example binaries (extensionless, next to their .wyn source)
multifile/src/math
multifile/src/strings
wynjs/src/runtime
wynjs/src/values
gui/*/src/main
server.db
wyn_cc_err.txt
# compiled binaries from wyn run (extensionless, next to source)
**/src/main
**/tests/test_*
!**/tests/test_*.wyn
!**/tests/test_*.js

# ---- wyncanvas ----
# Build artifact of wyncanvas/csrc/build.sh - regenerate with ./csrc/build.sh
wyncanvas/libwynimg/
wyncanvas/build/
wyncanvas/packages/
wyncanvas/wyn.lock
# Design docs and dogfooding findings live in the private internal-docs repo,
# never here: they cite absolute local paths, unshipped compiler internals, and
# forward roadmap. `specs/` matters as much as `plans/` - the wyncanvas spec was
# committed here once and had to be removed after the fact.
# Leading **/ matters: a bare `docs/superpowers/` is anchored to the repo ROOT and
# would not match `wyncanvas/docs/superpowers/`, which is where it actually was.
**/WYN_FINDINGS.md
**/docs/superpowers/
# Python bytecode from the math-lib wrapper's generated module
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --python / --shared build output: a shared library and its generated FFI wrapper.
# python/math-lib had a 227KB libmain.dylib and a generated main.py COMMITTED, built by a
# months-old compiler. A committed library keeps importing cleanly while the source drifts
# away from it, so the demo would go on "passing" without testing the current compiler at
# all - the same trap as a stale installed binary.
lib*.dylib
lib*.so
lib*.dll
python/math-lib/math_lib.py
